WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.600
ALBUM. Asset localization by unified matching.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:12.700
We reconstruct the lounge from video using Gaussian splatting. Glowing outlines show the retrieved assets in their saved positions.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.950
Each matched object is a reusable 3D asset.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.800
Here we query the foreground cane chair with a point in one of four input views.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:28.900
SAM appearance and Depth Anything Three geometry are combined across views into shared instance tokens.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:38.650
The matcher compares those tokens with reference views from the library. The recorded top five lead with the cane chair.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:48.350
The selected asset contributes its canonical surface geometry. The layout decoder uses the same instance tokens to estimate translation, rotation, and scale.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:54.050
In ScanNet Plus Plus, the input views reveal a dense color point cloud of each room.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:02.650
Watch the coffee table drawer slide out. In the kitchen, the refrigerator doors and wall cabinet open using the joints supplied with the assets.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:10.700
The office cabinet doors swing open and the desk drawers slide along their original rails.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:18.800
In this second office, the saved layout comes from checkpoint one hundred forty-seven K.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:28.650
In the lab kitchenette, the refrigerator and cabinets articulate in the room.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:39.350
With six views from Replica, ALBUM places assets across an open-plan room.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:50.250
At the window bar, the retrieved pendant lights and bar furniture sit in the original capture.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:01.450
We rigged the front door of this retrieved wardrobe to slide across the other panel.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:11.550
From above, the saved layouts show how objects are arranged in the captured rooms and in the held-out benchmark scenes.

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:19.550
The curated library includes textured and articulated meshes. Canonical renders of each asset are cached for matching.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:27.750
For training, the same camera follows an empty room as assets appear in their recorded poses.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:36.650
The camera moves inside two furnished apartments. Each rendered view shares the asset identities and three-dimensional layout of its room.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:43.050
Here are three more training rooms, viewed from their original panoramic cameras.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:51.600
Each highlighted instance links the image pixels to a library asset and a known position. These are the targets for learning to match and place objects.
